      "payload": {
        "findings": [
          {
            "affectedPaths": [
              "docs/workers/triage-worker.md",
              "packages/web/src/workers/triageWorker.js"
            ],
            "claim": "docs/workers/triage-worker.md's documented Job Flow omits the triage summary-comment step entirely, even though after this change every successfully triaged issue receives one by default (auto_comment defaults to true), leaving the worker's behavioral documentation incomplete relative to the now-unconditional comment posting.",
            "confidence": 0.7,
            "description": "Pre-existing omission, not a regression: the doc never claimed comments are not posted, so it is not a contradiction introduced by this PR. However, the fix makes comment posting a default-on behavior for every triaged issue (triageWorker.js:349-358, default true in packages/rules/src/schema.js:14), while the worker's own doc lists only label application and duplicate detection as post-classification actions (steps 7-8). Operators reading docs/workers/triage-worker.md will not learn that a bot comment is posted on every issue. Cosmetic/doc-only impact; no runtime defect.",
            "evidenceRefs": [
              "repo-read:docs/workers/triage-worker.md@HEAD:L8-L16",
              "repo-read:packages/web/src/workers/triageWorker.js@HEAD:L349-L358",
